IMPORT prelude

-- Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act 1958 (Singapore) -- what a corrosive substance is (s 2, First
-- Schedule), the offences (ss 3 to 8) and their punishments, the stop-and-search limit in s 9(3), and the presumptions (s 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation ("version in force from 17/8/2026"; retrieved 1 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CESOWA1958.txt.
-- Amendments annotated: Act 3 of 2021 wef 01/07/2025 (ss 2, 6(1A), 6(1B), 7(1A), 7(4), 12, Second Schedule deleted) and, the
-- latest, Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026 (ss 3, 6(1), 7(1)). The deposit shows the amended wording only, not what it replaced.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. REQ-0054: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the
-- Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The Act is short, so almost
-- all of it is encoded. Not encoded: s 9(1), (2) search powers beyond the s 9(3) limit, s 10 disposal of seized property, s 12
-- (the Minister's power to amend the First Schedule), what counts as an "offensive weapon", a "scheduled weapon" or a "prohibited
-- weapon" (the last two are defined in the Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021, which was not read), and the
-- consorting offences' "like punishment" beyond a comment.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act 1958`

§§ `2 and First Schedule -- corrosive substance`

-- s 2: "corrosive substance" means any of the acids and substances specified in the First Schedule, "and shall be deemed to include
-- all substances which are capable on application to the human body of causing hurt through corrosive action".
-- First Schedule: 1 sulphuric acid; 2 nitric acid; 3 hydrochloric acid; 4 formic acid; 5 acetic acid; 6 phenols; 7 ammonia;
-- 8 potassium hydroxide; 9 sodium hydroxide.
DECLARE Substance IS ONE OF
    `sulphuric acid`
    `nitric acid`
    `hydrochloric acid`
    `formic acid`
    `acetic acid`
    `phenols`
    `ammonia`
    `potassium hydroxide`
    `sodium hydroxide`
    `another substance capable of hurt through corrosive action`
    `a substance not capable of hurt through corrosive action`

GIVEN `the substance` IS A Substance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substance is a corrosive substance` IF
    CONSIDER `the substance`
    WHEN `a substance not capable of hurt through corrosive action` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 and 11(2) -- possession for the purpose of causing hurt`

-- s 3: any person who "carries or has in his possession or under his control any corrosive or explosive substance in circumstances
-- which raise a reasonable presumption that he intends to use or intends to enable some other person to use the substance for the
-- purpose of causing hurt" commits an offence: imprisonment up to 10 years, "and shall also be liable to caning".
-- s 11(2): in a prosecution under s 3 or 5, it is "presumed until the contrary is proved" that the substance was intended for causing
-- hurt if (a) the quantity exceeded what is reasonably required for ordinary household (or business) use; (b) it was kept concealed
-- or in a place other than where it might reasonably be expected to be kept; or (c) it was kept in a container other than one of a
-- kind in which it is ordinarily kept.
GIVEN `the quantity exceeded ordinary needs` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was concealed or in an unexpected place` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was in an unusual container` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11(2) presumes an intent to cause hurt` IF
        `the quantity exceeded ordinary needs`
    OR  `it was concealed or in an unexpected place`
    OR  `it was in an unusual container`

-- The two routes to the intent: the circumstances raise a reasonable presumption (s 3 itself), or an s 11(2) presumption arises and
-- the accused does not prove the contrary.
GIVEN `possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is corrosive or explosive` IS A BOOLEAN, `the circumstances raise a presumption of intent` IS A BOOLEAN, `an 11(2) presumption arises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused proves the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession is an offence under section 3` IF
        `possesses it`
    AND `it is corrosive or explosive`
    AND (    `the circumstances raise a presumption of intent`
         OR  (`an 11(2) presumption arises` AND (NOT `the accused proves the contrary`)))

§§ `11(1) -- the occupier of premises`

-- s 11(1): where a corrosive or explosive substance is found in or on premises, "the occupier of the premises shall be deemed to be
-- in possession of that substance unless he shall prove that some other person was in possession thereof, or that he had no
-- knowledge or reasonable means of knowledge that that substance was in or on the premises AND that he had taken all reasonable
-- precautions against that substance being kept" there.
GIVEN `it was found on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier proves another person possessed it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier proves no knowledge or means of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier proves all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier is deemed in possession` IF
        `it was found on the premises`
    AND (NOT `the occupier proves another person possessed it`)
    AND (NOT (`the occupier proves no knowledge or means of knowledge` AND `the occupier proves all reasonable precautions`))

§§ `4 -- using a corrosive or explosive substance or offensive weapon`

-- s 4: any person who "unlawfully and maliciously uses or attempts to use any corrosive substance or offensive weapon for the purpose
-- of causing hurt" or causes or attempts to cause an explosion likely to cause hurt "shall, whether any hurt has actually been caused
-- or not", be guilty: imprisonment for life "and shall also be punished with caning with not less than 6 strokes".
GIVEN `used or attempted to use it to cause hurt` IS A BOOLEAN, `unlawfully and maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN, `hurt was actually caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using is an offence under section 4` IF
    `used or attempted to use it to cause hurt` AND `unlawfully and maliciously`

§§ `5 and 8 -- consorting`

-- s 5 (corrosive or explosive substance, in contravention of s 3) and s 8(1) (offensive weapon, in contravention of s 6): any person
-- who "consorts with, or is found in the company of" the carrier, in circumstances raising "a reasonable presumption that he knew",
-- is guilty "unless he shall prove that he had reasonable grounds for believing" the carrying was "for a lawful purpose". The
-- punishment is "the like punishment as that other person". (Not modelled further: the consorter takes the carrier's penalty,
-- so a companion of someone carrying a prohibited weapon faces s 6(1A)'s mandatory caning.)
GIVEN `consorted with or was in the company of the carrier` IS A BOOLEAN, `the carrier was in contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `the circumstances raise a presumption that he knew` IS A BOOLEAN, `he proves reasonable grounds to believe the purpose lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consorting is an offence` IF
        `consorted with or was in the company of the carrier`
    AND `the carrier was in contravention`
    AND `the circumstances raise a presumption that he knew`
    AND (NOT `he proves reasonable grounds to believe the purpose lawful`)

§§ `6 -- carrying an offensive weapon in a public place`

-- s 6(1): any person who "in any public road or place carries or has in his possession or under his control any offensive weapon
-- otherwise than with lawful authority or for a lawful purpose": up to 3 years, "and shall also be liable to caning".
-- (1A): if it is "a prohibited weapon" under the Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021: up to 5 years "and shall also be
-- punished with caning with not less than 6 strokes".
-- (1B): "For the purposes of subsection (1) only, 'lawful purpose' INCLUDES" (a) use at work; (b) religious reasons; (c) theatrical
-- production or film-making for entertainment; (d) ornamental display; (e) slaughter or hunting of wild animals authorised under
-- written law; (f) gardening, animal husbandry or primary production. The list is open ("includes"): the encoding gives a value for
-- a purpose the court otherwise accepts, and treats "no purpose shown" as none.
-- (2): "the onus of proving the existence of a lawful purpose shall lie upon the accused".
-- (3): a weapon "shall be presumed to be carried with lawful authority" if carried (a) by a member of the SAF, the SPF or a lawfully
-- present visiting force; or (b) as part of official or ceremonial dress "on any official or ceremonial occasion".
DECLARE Carrier IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary member of the public`
    `a member of the Singapore Armed Forces`
    `a member of the Singapore Police Force`
    `a member of a lawfully present visiting force`
    `a person in ceremonial dress on a ceremonial occasion`
    `a person in ceremonial dress on no such occasion`

GIVEN `the carrier` IS A Carrier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lawful authority is presumed` IF
    CONSIDER `the carrier`
    WHEN `a member of the Singapore Armed Forces` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a member of the Singapore Police Force` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a member of a lawfully present visiting force` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person in ceremonial dress on a ceremonial occasion` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `use at work`
    `religious reasons`
    `a theatrical production or film`
    `an ornamental display`
    `authorised slaughter or hunting of wild animals`
    `gardening, animal husbandry or primary production`
    `another purpose the court accepts as lawful`
    `no purpose shown`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is lawful` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `no purpose shown` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `in a public road or place` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person carrying` IS A Carrier, `the stated purpose` IS A Purpose, `the accused proves the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying is an offence under section 6` IF
        `in a public road or place`
    AND (NOT `lawful authority is presumed` `the person carrying`)
    AND (NOT (`the purpose is lawful` `the stated purpose` AND `the accused proves the purpose`))

§§ `7 -- scheduled weapons`

-- s 7(1): any person who, "otherwise than for a lawful purpose", (a) carries or possesses, (b) manufactures, sells, hires or offers
-- them, or (c) lends or gives, any scheduled weapon: up to 5 years "and shall also be liable to caning"; for a second or subsequent
-- offence "not less than 2 years and not more than 8 years" and liable to caning.
-- (1A): the act is otherwise than for a lawful purpose IF (a) the person intends to injure or endanger another, cause reasonable fear
-- of injury, destroy or damage property, or facilitate another to do so, "and" (b) the possession is "(i) not authorised by a licence
-- or a class licence ...; (ii) not in accordance with the conditions of a licence or a class licence ...; and (iii) not exempt".
-- Read literally, all three of (b)(i) to (iii) must hold. The encoding takes the "and" at its word: a licence holder who breaches its
-- conditions meets (ii) but not (i). (An inference about how a court would read it is not attempted.)
-- (2): "the onus of proving the existence of a lawful purpose shall be upon the accused". The encoding reads (1A) as one route to an
-- unlawful purpose, and (2) as the other: failing to prove a lawful one.
GIVEN `intends injury, fear or damage` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence or class licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `acts within the licence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN, `is exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7(1A) makes the purpose unlawful` IF
        `intends injury, fear or damage`
    AND (NOT `holds a licence or class licence`)
    AND (NOT `acts within the licence conditions`)
    AND (NOT `is exempt`)

GIVEN `did a section 7(1) act with a scheduled weapon` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purpose is unlawful under 7(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused proves a lawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the scheduled weapon act is an offence` IF
        `did a section 7(1) act with a scheduled weapon`
    AND (`the purpose is unlawful under 7(1A)` OR (NOT `the accused proves a lawful purpose`))

-- (4): "second or subsequent offence" means the person is convicted of the current offence and "has been convicted or found guilty"
-- on at least one earlier occasion "within the period of 5 years immediately before the date on which the person is convicted" of the
-- current offence, of (i) the same offence under (1), or (ii) an offence under (1) as in force before the GEWCA 2021 commencement
-- "and that involved a scheduled weapon". The window runs conviction to conviction, not offence to offence.
DECLARE EarlierConviction IS ONE OF
    `the same offence under section 7(1)`
    `an old section 7(1) offence involving a scheduled weapon`
    `an old section 7(1) offence not involving a scheduled weapon`
    `an offence under section 6`

GIVEN `the earlier conviction` IS AN EarlierConviction, `years between the convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is a second or subsequent offence` IF
        `years between the convictions` AT MOST 5
    AND CONSIDER `the earlier conviction`
        WHEN `the same offence under section 7(1)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an old section 7(1) offence involving a scheduled weapon` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3, 4, 6, 7 -- punishments`

-- Collected from the sections quoted above. Every offence in the Act carries caning; ss 4 and 6(1A) make it mandatory with a minimum
-- of 6 strokes, the rest say "liable to caning". The consorting offences (ss 5, 8) take the carrier's punishment and are not listed.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `possession for causing hurt (s 3)`
    `using to cause hurt (s 4)`
    `carrying an offensive weapon in public (s 6(1))`
    `carrying a prohibited weapon in public (s 6(1A))`
    `a first scheduled weapon offence (s 7(1))`
    `a repeat scheduled weapon offence (s 7(1))`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment for life is the maximum` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using to cause hurt (s 4)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- For s 4 the Act sets no term of years: see `imprisonment for life is the maximum`. 0 is returned for it.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum term in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `possession for causing hurt (s 3)` THEN 10
    WHEN `carrying an offensive weapon in public (s 6(1))` THEN 3
    WHEN `carrying a prohibited weapon in public (s 6(1A))` THEN 5
    WHEN `a first scheduled weapon offence (s 7(1))` THEN 5
    WHEN `a repeat scheduled weapon offence (s 7(1))` THEN 8
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum term in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a repeat scheduled weapon offence (s 7(1))` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `caning is mandatory` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using to cause hurt (s 4)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `carrying a prohibited weapon in public (s 6(1A))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum strokes` MEANS
    IF `caning is mandatory` `the offence` THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `6(4), 7(3), 8(2) -- arrestable and non-bailable`

-- s 6(4), 7(3) and 8(2): the offence "shall be deemed to be an arrestable and non-bailable offence". Sections 3, 4 and 5 say nothing
-- of the kind; how the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 classifies them was not read.
DECLARE Section IS ONE OF
    `section 3`
    `section 4`
    `section 5`
    `section 6`
    `section 7`
    `section 8`

GIVEN `the section` IS A Section
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act deems the offence arrestable and non-bailable` IF
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 6` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 7` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 8` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `9(3) -- who may search a woman`

-- s 9(1), (2): a police officer may stop and search without warrant on "reasonable grounds for believing" that evidence of an offence
-- under the Act is likely to be found. (3): "No woman shall be searched under this section except by a woman."
GIVEN `the officer has reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person searched is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer searching is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the search is permitted` IF
        `the officer has reasonable grounds`
    AND ((NOT `the person searched is a woman`) OR `the officer searching is a woman`)
